name: Entry-point source facts remain readable and stale catalog recovery is explicit
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY OPENROUTER_API_KEY GEMINI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/entry_point_publication.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed @TMP_HOME
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
submit: scene
require-live-snap: 25 DATA-FLOW DIAGRAM | source-diagram
expect: PARTIAL
keys: Tab
require-live-snap: 25 ENTRY POINTS | source-entry-points
expect: Flask
expect: /health
keys: Down
require-live-snap: 25 FastAPI | second-source-route
resize: 160x48
live-snap: entries-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: entries-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: entries-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: entries-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: entries-40x12
keys: NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage NPage
wait: 3
live-snap: entries-tail-40x12
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/entry_point_publication.py @TMP_TARGET @ART tail
ask: Are source facts, provenance and navigation readable without claiming complete model validation across six sizes?
resize: 120x36
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 KUZUSHI | restored-origin
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/entry_point_publication.py @TMP_TARGET @ART drift
submit: run entry-points:extract {}
require-live-snap: 30 tree identity is stale | refused-stale-catalog
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/entry_point_publication.py @TMP_TARGET @ART stale
ask: Does failed extraction explain the stale source and preserve prior evidence without automatic rebuilding or provider work?
submit: run context:build {"enrichment":false}
require-live-snap: 35 This Map attempt produced no threat-model context | rebuilt-context
submit: run entry-points:extract {}
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/entry_point_publication.py @TMP_TARGET @ART await-rebuilt
require-live-snap: 35 RESULT READY | rebuilt-catalog
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/entry_point_publication.py @TMP_TARGET @ART rebuilt
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
submit: scene
require-live-snap: 25 DATA-FLOW DIAGRAM | restored-map
keys: Tab
require-live-snap: 25 Flask | restored-catalog
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/entry_point_publication.py @TMP_TARGET @ART rebuilt
ask: Does no-color restart show the rebuilt catalog and retain the prior Map's distinct source provenance without more work?
keys: Escape
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
